{"name":"Clay Bath","hex":"#8a7d69","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clay","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mineral substance made up of small crystals of silica and alumina, that is ductile when moist; the material of pre-fired ceramics.","An earth material with ductile qualities."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add clay to or to spread clay onto.","To purify using clay."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clay"},{"term":"bath","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tub or pool which is used for bathing: bathtub.","A building or area where bathing occurs."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To wash a person or animal in a bath.","To bathe (oneself); to have a bath."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bath"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clay","blocks":[{"text":"Clay is a type of fine-grained natural soil material containing clay minerals. Most pure clay minerals are white or light-coloured, but natural clays show a variety of colours from impurities, such as a reddish or brownish colour from small amounts of iron oxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Boulder_clay_cliff_south_of_Withernsea_%28geograph_6054962%29.jpg/330px-Boulder_clay_cliff_south_of_Withernsea_%28geograph_6054962%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clay"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Clay_magnified.jpg/500px-Clay_magnified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Clay_magnified.jpg/500px-Clay_magnified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 23,500 times magnified electron micrograph of smectite clay","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClay_magnified.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t